# (cheats_impl_report.md; Route B binary DmIOS.cheats.bin kept as the fallback): 46 hooks (39 BL + 7 B
# trampolines) minus 0x20636C (audit A2: leaf-returning site, the v4 BL stub dead-looped there, stays original)
# = 45 live stations, all executing from the patch area tail (guest 0x1ADB800..0x1ADBDAC, asserted unused by
# the rewriter). The engine flags live where the mini-stubs read them, in the unused bss slot 0x1A482C8
# (+1..+5 the QOL/LEVEL/DROP/WAR/RES groups), and dm/host writes them directly (dm_d3_flags_write in
# loader.c, called after relocation and from the gear menu's dm_setting_live on every toggle):
# DM_CHEAT_QOL/LEVEL/DROP/WAR/RES ("1"->1 else 0). High-risk cheats stay out of the 46 on purpose.
# v9 (Chen: no more probe builds - the next IPA must work): EVERY seasonal patch is removed. v2 (nxnative
# 46440957, zero guest patches) is the only build that ever entered the world; v3-v8 all carried subsets of
# the seasonal group and none did. The last common factor on the world-load path was 0x1BD140: it forced
# GameParams.season_created=30 for EVERY hero (0x1BD15C cbnz w21 then always took the seasonal branch),
# so offline world load waited on seasonal service data that never arrives - the loading screen spins at
# 60fps forever (v6 log: DecompressionThread idle, 60fps, no further progress until Chen backgrounded the
# app). The DM_SEASON_NUM launcher row stays but is inert until a later round designs offline seasons
# against d3hack's full five-piece set (XVar SetAndNotify + OnlineServicePTR spoof + event maps).
# v10 (Chen authorized the real offline-season port): lazy-init stubs. Two stubs hang off the first execution of
# Season::Num() (0x72E090) and IsSeasonsInitialized (0x5FF00) and preset the whole seasonal state BEFORE any reader
# sees it: XVar num/state = host menu slots (+7/+6 of the flag base, defaults 30/1), the initialized flag, the
# service-available gate, and seasons OverrideEnabled. Idempotent re-write on every call (aligned u32 stores are
# atomic; C++ static construction is guaranteed done because the trigger IS an XVar read). The create-flow gates
# (0x351CC4 UI, 0x61668 offline-true branch, 0x1BF5F0/94 ValidateHero, 0x56B10/14 sign-in always true) are point cuts; season_created (0x1BD140)
# and the spawn tbz (0x4CADB8) stay ORIGINAL - the hero's own data drives them. The journey detail opener
# (0x172C40) is neutered to ret: the journey data chain is server-fed dynamic objects and would NULL-crash
# (v6 evidence: 0x172d48); a later round can fake the container. World content itself is local SNO (the stock
# game keeps playing offline once loaded), so a seasonal hero should enter the world on the local path.
# Generated by d3_season/tools/rebuild_build.py; verify with rebuild_verify.py.
